### Public viewer share — guest surface + curator authz boundary (uc.sharing.share-public-viewer, cr-0100)
# Sharing is the first endpoint family with a genuinely UNAUTHENTICATED guest surface (ADR 0029): the
# anonymous resolve + gated blob GET are `@PermitAll`, gated only by share state. So unlike content.http /
# media / scopes (pure 401 walls), this file asserts REAL guest behavior — a well-formed but unknown share is
# a non-enumerable 404 (share_not_found, NOT a 401), which proves the guest paths are public and don't
# enumerate. The curator ops (create/list/revoke) are `@Authenticated` and asserted as 401 walls here.
#
# The full authenticated happy-path — create → anonymous resolve returns the sealed subtree → in-subtree blob
# GET authorized (503 store_unavailable on the dev store vs 404 out-of-subtree) → revoke → resolve 404 →
# expiry 404 → leaks-nothing-outside-the-subtree — is covered hermetically at the integration layer
# (ShareSliceTest, which seeds a member + personal scope + a Memory subtree in-tx) and end-to-end in the web
# client's live smoke (a real /s/ link opened with no session). Those need the operator-blind grant flow +
# client-side crypto, not reproducible from a bare .http. The **editable curator note** lifecycle (create with a
# note → resolve returns it → owner PATCH edits it in place at the same shareId → a non-owner PATCH is 404 →
# null clears it, cr-0115) is likewise covered hermetically by ShareNoteSliceTest; here we assert its auth wall.
#
# Run: ijhttp --env-file http/sharing/http-client.env.json --env dev http/sharing/sharing.http

### 1. Resolve a well-formed but unknown share with NO bearer → 404 share_not_found (public + non-enumerable)
# A 404 (not a 401) proves the resolve is @PermitAll: an account-less visitor reaches it, and an unknown id is
# indistinguishable from a disabled/expired one (no enumeration). The id is a valid 43-char base64url shape.
GET {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA

> {%
client.test("unknown share resolves to a public, non-enumerable 404", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 404, "expected 404, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "share_not_found", "expected share_not_found");
});
%}

### 2. Gated blob GET on an unknown share with NO bearer → 404 (public; the subtree gate reveals nothing)
GET {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA/blobs/9b1d4a6e-8b2c-1f2d-3e4a-5b6c7c3f0e2a

> {%
client.test("gated blob GET on an unknown share is a public 404", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 404, "expected 404, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "share_not_found", "expected share_not_found");
});
%}

### 3. Create a share without a bearer token → 401 (curator op; auth before validation)
POST {{host}}/api/shares
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nodeId": "4a6e8b2c-1f2d-3e4a-5b6c-7c3f0e2a9b1d", "role": "VIEWER", "wrap": "d3JhcA==", "sealedName": "c2VhbGVk" }

> {%
client.test("create share requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 4. List the caller's shares without a bearer token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/shares

> {%
client.test("list shares requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 5. Revoke a share without a bearer token → 401 (curator op)
POST {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA/revoke

> {%
client.test("revoke share requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 6. Re-activate a share without a bearer token → 401 (curator op, cr-0104)
POST {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA/reactivate

> {%
client.test("reactivate share requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 7. Edit a share's note without a bearer token → 401 (curator op, cr-0115; auth before validation)
PATCH {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sealedNote": "bm90ZS12Mg==" }

> {%
client.test("update share note requires auth", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 401, "expected 401, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "authentication_failed", "expected authentication_failed");
});
%}

### 8. Resolve an unknown share WITH an X-Share-Password header → still 404 (cr-0118: the password gate is after
### the existence check, so the header is not an enumeration oracle — a bad id reveals nothing, password or not).
### The authed password happy-path (locked resolve → wrong then right token → content) is slice-proven
### (SharePasswordSliceTest) — it needs a real member-scope share the boundary file can't create.
GET {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA
X-Share-Password: cHctdG9rZW4=

> {%
client.test("a password header on an unknown share still 404s (non-enumerable)", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 404, "expected 404, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "share_not_found", "expected share_not_found");
});
%}
